licensed under Apache-2.0.

What changed, in substance:

  - Two exploitable SSRF flaws in the upstream egress path were fixed: IPv6
    literals bypassing the private-range check, and DNS rebinding between
    validation and fetch. Both are documented with the vulnerable pattern and
    the fix in docs/security.md, and were disclosed to the upstream maintainer.
  - The upstream's open ?url= tile proxy, itself a request-forgery primitive,
    was replaced with a host allowlist.
  - stealthFetch — which rotated forged X-Forwarded-For and User-Agent headers
    to evade upstream rate limits — was removed. This fork identifies itself
    honestly on every request.
  - Fabricated data was removed. The upstream's cyber layer animated simulated
    attacks; this fork serves clearly-labelled reference data and reports
    unavailable sources as unavailable.
  - Non-commercially-licensed feeds were replaced with sources whose terms
    permit commercial display. Every source, with its licence, is inventoried in
    docs/data-sources.md — including the ones we rejected and why.
  - The cryptocurrency token panel and donation solicitations were removed.
  - Module-level caches, rate limiters and timers were replaced with a pluggable
    KV store, so the app is correct when run as more than one instance.
  - A provider-agnostic AI analyst routed through a configurable model gateway
    replaces the hard-wired Google SDK dependency.

